---
import MainLayout from '@/layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import StaticPage from '@/components/ui/StaticPage.astro';

const title = 'Terms of use';
const description = 'The ground rules for using Glitch.';
---

<MainLayout title={title} description={description}>
  <StaticPage
    title="Terms of use"
    intro="A few ground rules so Glitch stays a decent place to talk about games."
  >
    <h2>Using Glitch</h2>
    <p>
      Glitch is provided as-is for personal, non-commercial use. You need an account to write
      reviews, comment, and follow other players; browsing the catalogue and reading reviews does
      not require one.
    </p>

    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <p>
      Keep your password to yourself and your account details accurate. You are responsible for what
      is posted from your account.
    </p>

    <h2>What you post</h2>
    <p>Reviews, comments, and ratings are public. When you post, you agree not to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Harass, threaten, or target other people.</li>
      <li>Post hate speech, spam, or advertising.</li>
      <li>Publish content you do not have the right to share.</li>
      <li>Use the platform to break the law.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      We may remove content or suspend accounts that break these rules. An admin panel exists
      specifically so reviews and users can be moderated.
    </p>

    <h2>Game data</h2>
    <p>
      Game titles, artwork, and metadata belong to their respective owners and are sourced from
      IGDB. Glitch claims no ownership over them.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      These terms may change as the project evolves. Continued use after a change means you accept
      the updated version.
    </p>

    <p>
      Questions? See <a href="/help">Help centre</a> or <a href="/support">Support</a>.
    </p>
  </StaticPage>
</MainLayout>
